  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 919723,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "Active Support's number helpers accepted strings in scientific notation. `BigDecimal` parses a string such as `\"11288E822220222\"` into a number with hundreds of trillions of digits, and formatting that number exhausts memory or ties up the CPU. An application that passes user input to `number_to_currency`, `number_to_percentage` or another number helper can be taken down by a single request.\n\n[CVE-2026-33176](https://github.com/rails/rails/security/advisories/GHSA-2j26-frm8-cmj9) fixes this in Active Support 7.2.3.1, 8.0.4.1 and 8.1.2.1. The helpers now treat any string containing `e` or `d` as non-numeric and return it unchanged, as they already did for other non-numeric input.\n\nThanks to @manun for the report.",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-06T18:43:20.541Z",
